title: Economic Democracy
is-card: true
new-page: true
on-arrival: economic_democracy_timer += 10; month_actions += 1
view-if: psoe_in_government and (economic_minister_party == "PSOE" or finance_minister_party == "PSOE") and labor_minister_party == "PSOE" and economic_democracy_timer <= 0
card-image: img/portraits/HilferdingRudolf.jpg
max-visits: 8
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
#subtitle: How can we give workers more control over the means of production?

= Economic Democracy

A key part of the <span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> platform is that workers should have more control over the economy. This can be done either directly at the enterprise level, through factory committees with real influence over management, or indirectly via the democratic government, by acquiring key industries from the capitalist class and placing them under democratic control.

As we control the Labor [? if economic_minister_party == "PSOE" : and Economy ?][? if finance_minister_party == "PSOE" : and Finance ?] ministries, we can finally begin to implement our long-standing goals. [? if in_republican_socialist or in_popular_front: Our republican coalition partners might not agree, however. ?]

- @expand_councils
- @expand_councils_2
- @expand_councils_3
- @nationalize_1
- @cooperatives_1
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@expand_councils
title: Support factory committees.
subtitle: Give factory committees a greater influence in managing enterprises.
view-if: works_councils == 0
on-arrival: economic_democracy += 1; industrial_psoe += 7*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress += 1; works_councils += 1; labor_dissent -= 6; labor_strength += 8; radical_relation -= 5; izq_rep_relation -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1
max-visits: 1

Factory committees, elected by workers at each major enterprise, have existed in name since the Republic's founding, but they have been largely powerless in the face of capital. Now, we will secure worker representation on company boards, giving them real influence over management decisions.


@expand_councils_2
title: Support sectoral and national factory committees.
subtitle: This is a step towards workers' control over the entire economy.
view-if: works_councils == 1
on-arrival: economic_democracy += 1; industrial_psoe += 7*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress += 1; works_councils += 1; labor_dissent -= 6; labor_strength += 8; radical_relation -= 5; izq_rep_relation -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1; economic_growth += 0.1 if economic_growth < 3
max-visits: 1

The Constitution promises workers a voice in the economy, but so far the factory committees have been little more than advisory bodies. We can change that, linking them into sectoral and national bodies with real standing.


@expand_councils_3
title: Empower sectoral factory committees.
subtitle: Give factory committees a role in setting wage and price policy for entire industrial sectors.
view-if: works_councils == 2
on-arrival: economic_democracy += 1; industrial_psoe += 7*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress += 1; works_councils += 1; labor_dissent -= 6; labor_strength += 8; radical_relation -= 5; izq_rep_relation -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1; unemployed -= 2 if unemployed > 5; economic_growth += 0.1 if economic_growth < 3
max-visits: 1

Sectoral factory committees can now negotiate wage and price policy for entire economic sectors, giving workers a real voice while also helping to rationalize production, smoothing over the anarchy of the market.

@nationalize_1
title: Begin to socialize key industries.
subtitle: -1 budget - we should buy out industries and govern them together with workers and consumers.
on-arrival: economic_democracy += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; budget -= 1; socializations += 1; industrial_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if black_thursday_seen; unemployed -= 1 if unemployed > 9; radical_relation -= 3; izq_rep_relation -= 3; ceda_relation -= 3; economic_growth += 0.2 if economic_growth < 5
choose-if: budget >= 1
max-visits: 3

We have begun to socialize key industries by buying out the capitalist owners, and creating coordinated governing boards with worker, consumer, and state representatives. The propertied classes are not pleased at our intrusion into the economy.

@cooperatives_1
title: Support worker and consumer cooperatives.
subtitle: -1 budget
on-arrival: economic_democracy += 1; cooperatives += 1; industrial_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); budget -= 1; unemployed -= 1 if unemployed > 9; economic_growth += 0.2
choose-if: budget >= 1
max-visits: 3

We have enacted legislation that makes it easier to form cooperative enterprises of all sorts, and provide financial support to struggling cooperatives.
